## OptionalDeps: GatherMate2_Data

# Load order is load-bearing, not stylistic.
#
# Every file binds the modules it depends on at file scope (local Data = NS.Data).
# List one too early and it doesn't error -- it quietly gets nil, and you find out
# about it three zones later.
#
#   Constants   enums, colors, defaults. Depends on nobody.
#   Species     GENERATED: every gathering node in the game, its expansion, and
#               every name it can wear. Data only; depends on nobody but Constants.
#   Database    what we remember, how far, which way, and the filter gate
#   Seed        SOURCE: somebody else's map (GatherMate2_Data), if it's installed.
#               Needs Data. Optional at runtime; we bundle none of it.
#   Live        SOURCE: the soft-interact target -- the ONLY thing that can tell us
#               a node is really there. Needs Data and Seed (Seed is how it knows
#               WHERE the thing it found is). This is the default cue.
#   Hud         THE POINT: your minimap, moved to the middle of the screen with
#               the terrain masked off, leaving only the game's own tracking
#               blips. Owns no data and no timer -- it just relocates a frame.
#   Corner      ...and what goes in the hole it left: Blizzard's Battlefield Map
#               (a MapCanvas), parked where the minimap was and locked to you.
#               Needs the tray Hud builds, so it loads after it.
#   Vignettes   what we can actually SEE (treasures). Needs Data.
#   Overlay     RENDERER: the radar. Opt-in now -- see NS.db.mode.
#   Cue         RENDERER: the thing in the middle of your screen. The point.
#   Scan        THE ENGINE: one look around per tick, handed to the renderers.
#               Loads after them, because it's the only file that needs them.
#   Options     the knobs
#   Core        wakes everything up. Assumes the rest exists, so it goes last.
Constants.lua
Species.lua
Database.lua
Seed.lua
Live.lua
Vignettes.lua
Hud.lua
Corner.lua
Overlay.lua
Cue.lua
Scan.lua
Options.lua
Core.lua

# NOTE: Bindings.xml is NOT listed here on purpose. The client auto-loads a file
# named exactly "Bindings.xml" from the addon folder and feeds it to the KEYBINDING
# parser. List it here and the UI-XML parser grabs it instead, doesn't understand
# <Binding>, and spits "Unrecognized XML" warnings. See Escape > Keybindings.

# --- Bumping for 12.1 ----------------------------------------------------------
# Change Interface to 120100 when the patch lands. Several at once is fine:
#   ## Interface: 120007, 120100
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- No libraries ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Eyes Up needs no libraries and never will.
#
# It used to list HereBeDragons as an OptionalDeps, and used it for true yards
# when it happened to be installed. It turned out the client answers the only
# question we were asking it -- C_Map.GetMapWorldSize gives a zone's real size in
# yards, per axis, for free. See Data.MapSize. One code path, no dependency, and
# a yard is now a yard whether or not you have anything else installed.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
